            <title>[LU-21204] -c 40 stripping lead to 7 stripes, instead of 8 (with 8-OSTs system)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21204</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;A plain component whose stripe count is larger than the number of OSTs is clamped to the OST count and flagged LOD_USES_DEFAULT_STRIPE, so only 3/4 of the count has to be found before allocation succeeds.  lod_ost_alloc_rr() keeps its first pass off the OSTs used by another component of the file and retried only while short of that minimum, so  a trailing PFL component could stop one OST short: -c 40 on an 8-OST file system, with one OST taken by an earlier component, allocated 7  stripes instead of 8 and capped the file at 112 TB, while -c 8 reused the OST and got all 8.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
